  "result": "Excellent! All 223 tests pass. I've successfully implemented voucher functionality for the invoicing system:\n\n**Added to src/errors.js:**\n- `VOUCHER_EXISTS` \u2014 for attempting to apply multiple vouchers to an invoice\n\n**Updated src/invoices.js:**\n- `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` \u2014 applies a fixed-amount voucher to a draft invoice:\n  - Validates invoice is in draft status (NOT_DRAFT error if not)\n  - Validates only one voucher per invoice (VOUCHER_EXISTS error if already present)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID error otherwise)\n  - Returns ok(newInvoice) with invoice.voucher = { code, amount }\n  - Does not mutate the original invoice\n  \n- `invoiceTotals(invoice)` \u2014 now includes voucher amount:\n  - Returns { subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }\n  - total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher (clamped at 0)\n  - Voucher is 0 if not present on invoice\n\n- All invoice operations (`addLine`, `removeLine`, `issueInvoice`) now preserve voucher data\n\n**Updated src/payments.js:**\n- `recordPayment` preserves voucher in returned invoice\n\n**Comprehensive test coverage (223 tests total; 17 new):**\n- Valid voucher application and error cases\n- Voucher interaction with discounts and VAT\n- Voucher preservation through all operations\n- Non-mutation of original invoices\n- Edge cases (large vouchers, vouchers exceeding totals)\n\nAll house rules followed: no argument mutation, Result pattern for errors, amount validation, all tests passing.",
